<title>USA: Mountasia may take Q4 charge.</title>
<headline>Mountasia may take Q4 charge.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mountasia Entertainment International Inc said it may sell or close some 16 parks and take a minimum charge of $8.2 million in its fourth quarter.</p>
<p>The company said the charge could be as much as $15.7 million if it closes or sells another eight parks that are now under review.</p>
<p>The 16 parks to be sold or closed during the next few months had revenue of $5 million for the period ended September 30, resulting in a loss of $400,000, the company said. The eight additional parks had a loss of $800,000 on revenue of $4.7 million, the company said.</p>
</text>
